WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:15.180
Nat stood at the door of Jo's study and peered inside.

2
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.421
"Please, ma'am, may I speak to you about something very important?"

3
00:00:20.721 --> 00:00:26.423
Nat was the third boy who'd interrupted Jo in the last half hour, but she was used to

4
00:00:26.463 --> 00:00:29.884
distractions. "What is it, my boy?"

5
00:00:30.264 --> 00:00:30.824
she asked.

6
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:35.441
Nat entered, shutting the door carefully behind him.

7
00:00:37.281 --> 00:00:39.142
"Dan's here," he said eagerly.

8
00:00:39.162 --> 00:00:41.023
"Who's Dan?"

9
00:00:41.303 --> 00:00:42.003
Jo asked.

10
00:00:42.023 --> 00:00:45.324
"A boy I knew when I played the fiddle in the city.

11
00:00:46.504 --> 00:00:49.945
He's 14, and he sold newspapers and was always kind to me.

12
00:00:51.345 --> 00:00:52.206
Last week when Mr.

13
00:00:52.246 --> 00:00:55.367
Laurence took me to a concert in the city, I saw Dan on the street.

14
00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:59.788
I told him how nice it was here, and now he's come to see for himself."

15
00:01:01.636 --> 00:01:06.638
"This is a rather unexpected visit," Jo murmured, pushing back her chair.

16
00:01:06.658 --> 00:01:10.900
"Oh, this isn't a visit—Dan has come to stay!"

17
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:12.040
Nat said.

18
00:01:13.281 --> 00:01:17.462
But when he caught the startled look on Jo's face, he corrected himself.

19
00:01:17.482 --> 00:01:20.964
"I mean, if you'll allow him to stay."

20
00:01:20.984 --> 00:01:30.828
"Well, I don't know about that yet," Jo began, caught off guard by the suddenness of this proposal.

21
00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:35.474
"I thought you liked to take care of poor boys like me," Nat said.

22
00:01:35.494 --> 00:01:42.278
"I do, but I can't take in every boy who comes to our door—there isn't room.

23
00:01:43.518 --> 00:01:45.980
Besides, I like to choose who lives here."

24
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.502
"Dan could have my bed, and I could sleep in the barn," Nat said.

25
00:01:50.522 --> 00:01:53.604
"I used to sleep anywhere with my father."

26
00:01:55.085 --> 00:02:00.548
Jo was touched by Nat's confidence in her, and she didn't have the heart to spoil his plan.

27
00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:05.002
"Bring him in, and we'll try to find space for him."

28
00:02:06.823 --> 00:02:13.667
Nat happily ran off and soon returned, followed by a tall boy who gave Jo a hostile look

29
00:02:13.747 --> 00:02:15.748
from underneath his long black hair.

30
00:02:16.849 --> 00:02:19.710
She instantly sensed he was a troublemaker.

31
00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:23.513
"This is Dan," Nat said.

32
00:02:23.533 --> 00:02:29.196
"Nat tells me you'd like to stay with us," Jo began in a friendly tone.

33
00:02:30.664 --> 00:02:33.005
"It sounds like you don't have anywhere else to go?"

34
00:02:33.025 --> 00:02:39.448
"Nope." "Say, 'No, ma'am,'" Nat whispered.

35
00:02:39.468 --> 00:02:41.329
"I won't!"

36
00:02:41.829 --> 00:02:42.609
Dan muttered.

37
00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:46.991
Jo ignored this conversation and went on.

38
00:02:47.011 --> 00:02:52.414
"If you stay here, we'll expect you to work and study as well as play.

39
00:02:53.774 --> 00:02:55.135
Are you willing to agree to that?"

40
00:02:55.155 --> 00:02:57.416
"Don't mind trying."

41
00:02:59.264 --> 00:03:02.325
"You can stay a few days, and we'll see how we get along."

42
00:03:03.785 --> 00:03:07.847
Jo had never met a boy with such a hard, suspicious face.

43
00:03:07.867 --> 00:03:12.928
"Please take him outside, Nat, and introduce him to the other boys."

44
00:03:12.948 --> 00:03:14.789
"Thank you, ma'am!"

45
00:03:15.209 --> 00:03:15.809
Nat said.

46
00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:21.691
Outside, Nat led Dan to the barn.

47
00:03:21.711 --> 00:03:24.672
"We're having a circus!"

48
00:03:25.032 --> 00:03:25.472
he said.

49
00:03:26.416 --> 00:03:29.577
Nat and Dan joined Rob and Jack in the audience.

50
00:03:31.418 --> 00:03:34.578
Bales of hay marked a wide circle on the barn floor.

51
00:03:35.659 --> 00:03:41.821
Demi stood in the middle with a whip, while Tommy rode Toby the donkey, pretending he was a

52
00:03:41.881 --> 00:03:50.623
horse. The next act featured Jack dancing a fine jig, and then Tommy proudly turned a somersault, a

53
00:03:50.683 --> 00:03:52.604
trick he'd been working on for weeks.

54
00:03:55.148 --> 00:03:56.728
"That's not really a trick!"

55
00:03:57.609 --> 00:03:58.809
Dan said, laughing.

56
00:03:58.829 --> 00:04:03.570
"Hey!" Tommy scowled as he rubbed his sore elbows.

57
00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:06.291
"Don't insult me!"

58
00:04:06.311 --> 00:04:14.754
"I'll insult whoever I want," Dan said, approaching Tommy and holding up his fists like he meant business.

59
00:04:14.774 --> 00:04:16.814
"Do you want to fight?"

60
00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:22.496
"Uh, not really," Tommy muttered and took a step back.

61
00:04:24.556 --> 00:04:26.457
"Fighting isn't allowed!"

62
00:04:26.777 --> 00:04:27.657
the others cried.

63
00:04:27.677 --> 00:04:32.860
"Well, aren't you a nice little group," Dan said with a sneer.

64
00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:41.023
"If you don't behave, Dan, you won't be allowed to stay," Nat said, annoyed that Dan was insulting

65
00:04:41.083 --> 00:04:41.704
his friends.

66
00:04:41.724 --> 00:04:46.506
"I'd just like to see him perform better than I did," Tommy said.

67
00:04:46.526 --> 00:04:49.907
"Get out of the way then!"

68
00:04:50.268 --> 00:04:57.214
Dan replied, barely pausing before he turned three somersaults, one after the other, and landed on his feet.

69
00:04:57.234 --> 00:05:01.655
"You can't beat that, Tommy," Nat said.

70
00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:09.677
Before Nat could say another word, Dan did three backward somersaults followed by a short walk on his

71
00:05:09.717 --> 00:05:17.940
hands. This impressed everyone, and even Tommy joined in the cries of admiration.

72
00:05:19.328 --> 00:05:22.950
Dan looked at his audience with an air of calm superiority.

73
00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:26.792
"Do you think I could learn to do that without getting hurt?"

74
00:05:27.013 --> 00:05:28.073
Tommy asked Dan.

75
00:05:28.093 --> 00:05:31.235
"What will you give me if I teach you?"

76
00:05:32.976 --> 00:05:36.678
"My new pocket knife has five blades, and only one is broken."

77
00:05:36.698 --> 00:05:39.160
"Hand it over."

78
00:05:41.101 --> 00:05:46.684
Tommy reluctantly gave his knife to Dan, who examined it and started to walk away.

79
00:05:48.396 --> 00:05:55.242
"Here's my advice: keep practicing until you learn how to do it."

80
00:05:55.302 --> 00:06:00.246
A howl of wrath from Tommy was followed by everyone running after Dan.

81
00:06:00.266 --> 00:06:02.788
"Give him back his knife right now!"

82
00:06:03.188 --> 00:06:03.829
Nat said.

83
00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:08.513
After Dan obeyed, Nat grabbed Dan's arm.

84
00:06:08.533 --> 00:06:11.695
"And now you're going for a walk with me!"

85
00:06:14.858 --> 00:06:21.691
No one knew what Nat said to Dan, but when they reappeared, Dan was more respectful toward everyone.

86
00:06:23.212 --> 00:06:28.835
The boys still didn't like Dan and left him to Nat, who soon felt burdened by his old

87
00:06:28.915 --> 00:06:31.797
friend. When Mr.

88
00:06:31.857 --> 00:06:35.559
Bauer heard the story of Dan's first day, he shook his head.

89
00:06:35.579 --> 00:06:40.942
"We may have made a mistake by taking him in," he said to Jo.

90
00:06:40.962 --> 00:06:44.304
"But only time will tell."

91
00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:53.344
As time passed, Jo lost her patience with Dan half a dozen times a day, but she didn't

92
00:06:53.404 --> 00:06:54.205
give up on him.

93
00:06:54.225 --> 00:07:00.709
"I know there's some good inside Dan," she said to her husband.

94
00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:06.694
"He may be rude to people, but he's kind to animals, and Teddy is so fond of him."

95
00:07:08.455 --> 00:07:09.115
It was true.

96
00:07:09.616 --> 00:07:14.099
Dan was very affectionate with little Teddy, who called him my Danny.

97
00:07:15.119 --> 00:07:19.462
To Jo, these were signs that she could eventually win Dan over.
